hadiths[83]{hadithnumber,text}:
"3122","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Guard the prayers of the two times: the prayer before sunrise and the prayer before sunset."
"3123","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Love for the Ansar is a sign of faith, and hatred of the Ansar is a sign of a hypocrite."
"3124","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Of your world, women and fragrance have been made beloved to me, and the coolness of my eyes has been placed in prayer."
"3125","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""How excellent are those of my Ummah who use the toothpick (khilal)."
"3126","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""The Fire has been veiled with desires, and Paradise has been veiled with things that are disliked."
"3127","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Perform Hajj on behalf of your father, and perform Umrah as well."
"3128","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""First perform Hajj for yourself, then perform Hajj on behalf of Shubrumah."
"3129","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""The width of a road is seven cubits."
"3130","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""A prescribed punishment (hadd) carried out on the earth is better for the people of the earth than for rain to fall upon them for forty days."
"3131","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Narrate the accounts of the Children of Israel; there is no harm in it."
"3132","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Making profit on something for which liability has not been assumed is unlawful."
"3133","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Whatever intoxicates in a large quantity, even a small quantity of it is unlawful."
"3134","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Allah Almighty has made wine unlawful, and every intoxicant is unlawful."
"3135","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Every person who is gentle in temperament, soft-hearted, easy-going and close to the people is forbidden to the Fire."
"3136","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""The Fire touching two eyes has been made forbidden: an eye that wept out of the fear of Allah, and an eye that stayed awake all night guarding Islam and the people of Islam from the disbelievers."
"3137","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Wearing silk and gold has been made unlawful for the men of my Ummah and lawful for their women."
"3138","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""The area between the two stony tracts of Madinah has been declared sacred upon my tongue."
"3139","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Trading in wine has been made unlawful."
"3140","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""The sanctity of a Muslim's wealth is like the sanctity of his blood."
"3141","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""The sanctity of the wives of the mujahidin upon those who stay at home is like the sanctity of their own mothers. And any man who stays at home and looks after the family of one of the mujahidin in his absence, and then betrays him regarding them, will be made to stand before the mujahid on the Day of Resurrection, and it will be said to him: 'This man looked after your family in your absence, so take from his good deeds as much as you wish.' So he will take from his deeds as much as he wishes. So what do you think?"
"3142","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""The protected area (harim) of a date palm extends as far as the reach of its branches."
"3143","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Sufficient for you among the women of the worlds are these: Maryam bint Imran, Khadijah bint Khuwaylid, Fatimah bint Muhammad, and Asiyah the wife of Pharaoh."
"3144","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""A beautiful voice is the adornment of the Qur'an."
"3145","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Beautify the Qur'an with your voices, for a beautiful voice increases the Qur'an in beauty."
"3146","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Husayn is from me and I am from Husayn. May Allah love whoever loves Husayn. Hasan and Husayn are two grandsons among the grandsons."
"3147","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Paradise has been surrounded with disliked things, and the Fire has been surrounded with desires."
"3148","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""The right of a husband over his wife is so great that if he had a wound and she licked it, she would still not have fulfilled his right."
"3149","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""The right of the wife over the husband is that he feeds her when he himself eats, clothes her when he himself dresses, does not strike the face, does not revile her, and if he must express his displeasure, he does so only within the home."
"3150","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""The Muslim has five rights over the Muslim: returning the greeting of salam, visiting the sick, following the funeral, accepting the invitation, and responding to the one who sneezes."
"3151","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""The Muslim has six rights over the Muslim: when you meet him, greet him with salam; when he invites you, accept; when he seeks your advice, advise him; when he sneezes and says Alhamdulillah, respond to him; when he falls ill, visit him; and when he dies, follow his funeral."
"3152","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Whoever marries seeking chastity, to keep away from what Allah has forbidden, it is a right upon Allah to help him."
"3153","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""It is a right upon every Muslim to use the miswak, to take a ritual bath (ghusl) on Friday, and to apply perfume if there is any in his household."
"3154","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""It is a right of Allah upon every Muslim that he takes a ritual bath (ghusl) one day in every seven days, in which he washes his head and his body."
"3155","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""The sweetness of this world is the bitterness of the Hereafter, and the bitterness of this world is the sweetness of the Hereafter."
"3156","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""The ally of a people is one of them, and the sister's son of a people is also one of them."
"3157","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Hamzah bin Abd al-Muttalib is my foster brother."
"3158","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Hamzah is the leader of the martyrs on the Day of Resurrection."
"3159","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""A man from among those who came before you was brought to account, and no good deed was found for him except that he was a wealthy man who dealt with people, and he used to order his servants to grant respite to the one in hardship. So Allah, the Mighty and Majestic, said to His angels: 'We are more entitled to that than he is; forgive him.'"
"3160","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""My Pool is as wide as the distance between Sana'a and Madinah; in it are vessels shining like the stars."
"3161","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""My Pool is a month's journey across, its sides are equal, its water is whiter than milk, its fragrance is finer than musk, and its cups are like the stars of the sky. Whoever drinks from it will never be thirsty."
"3162","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""My Pool stretches from Aden to Amman of al-Balqa. Its water is whiter than milk and sweeter than honey, and its cups are as numerous as the stars of the sky. Whoever drinks a single draught from it will never be thirsty after it. The first people to arrive at it will be the poor among the Muhajirun, with dishevelled hair and soiled clothes, who cannot marry women accustomed to luxury, and for whom the doors of the wealthy are not opened."
"3163","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""We too hum around that."
"3164","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Wherever you may be, send blessings upon me, for your blessings reach me."
"3165","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Wherever you pass by the grave of a disbeliever, give him the tidings of the Fire."
"3166","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""When a menstruating woman and a woman in postnatal bleeding reach the miqat, they should take a ritual bath (ghusl), enter the state of ihram, and perform all the rites of Hajj except the circumambulation (tawaf) of the Ka'bah."
"3167","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""The pilgrim is the one with dishevelled hair who is without perfume."
"3168","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""In black seed there is healing for every disease except death."
"3169","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Cupping on an empty stomach is best; in it there is healing and blessing, and it increases memory and intellect. So have cupping done, with the blessing of Allah, on Thursday, and avoid cupping on Friday, Saturday and Sunday. Have cupping done on Monday and Tuesday, for that is the day on which Allah healed Ayyub (peace be upon him) from his affliction. And avoid cupping on Wednesday, for that is the day on which Ayyub (peace be upon him) was afflicted, and leprosy and leucoderma appear only on Wednesday or on the night of Wednesday."
"3170","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""There is no reward for an accepted Hajj (Hajj Mabrur) except Paradise."
"3171","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Hajj is the jihad of every weak person."
"3172","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Hajj is standing at Arafah. Whoever arrives before the break of dawn on the night of Muzdalifah has attained the Hajj. The days of Mina are three; so whoever hastens in two days, there is no sin upon him, and whoever delays, there is no sin upon him either."
"3173","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Those performing Hajj and those performing Umrah are the guests of Allah. He called them and they answered Him, and they asked of Him and He gave them."
"3174","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""The Black Stone is from Paradise."
"3175","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""The Black Stone is one of the stones of Paradise."
"3176","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""War is deception."
"3177","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Silk is the clothing of the one who has no share in the Hereafter."
"3178","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Noble standing (hasab) is in reality wealth, and honour (karam) is in reality piety (taqwa)."
"3179","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Hasan is from me and Husayn is from Ali."
"3180","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Hasan and Husayn are the leaders of the youth of the people of Paradise."
"3181","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Hasan and Husayn are the leaders of the youth of the people of Paradise, except for the two maternal cousins, Isa bin Maryam and Yahya bin Zakariyya; and Fatimah is the leader of the women of the people of Paradise, except for Maryam bint Imran."
"3182","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Hasan and Husayn are the leaders of the youth of the people of Paradise, and their father is better than them both."
"3183","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Swearing oaths makes merchandise sell, but it wipes out the blessing."
"3184","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""'All praise is for Allah, the Lord of all the worlds' is the Mother of the Qur'an, the Mother of the Book, and the Seven Oft-Repeated Verses."
"3185","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""'All praise is for Allah, the Lord of all the worlds' is the Seven Oft-Repeated Verses that I have been given, and it is the Magnificent Qur'an."
"3186","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Fever is the believer's share of Hell on the Day of Resurrection."
"3187","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Fever is every believer's share of Hell."
"3188","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Fever is from the furnace of Hell; so whatever fever afflicts the believer is his share of Hell."
"3189","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Fever is from the furnace of Hell; so drive it away from yourselves with cold water."
"3190","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Fever is from the furnace of Hell, and it is the believer's share of Hell."
"3191","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Fever is from the heat of Hell; so cool it with water."
"3192","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""The bathhouse is forbidden for the women of my Ummah."
"3193","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""The lawful is clear and the unlawful is clear, and between them are doubtful matters which many people do not know. So whoever guards himself against the doubtful matters has safeguarded his religion and his honour, and whoever falls into the doubtful matters falls into the unlawful, like a shepherd who grazes his animals around a protected pasture, about to stray into it. Beware! Every king has a protected pasture. Beware! The protected pasture of Allah Almighty on His earth is the things He has forbidden. Beware! In the body there is a piece of flesh; if it is sound, the whole body is sound, and if it is corrupt, the whole body is corrupt. Beware! It is the heart."
"3194","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""The lawful is clear and the unlawful is clear; so leave what makes you doubt for what does not make you doubt."
"3195","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""The lawful is what Allah has made lawful in His Book, and the unlawful is what Allah has made unlawful in His Book, and whatever He remained silent about is among the things He has pardoned."
"3196","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Modesty is entirely good."
"3197","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Modesty is part of faith."
"3198","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Modesty is part of faith, and the most modest of my Ummah is Uthman."
"3199","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Modesty is part of faith, and faith leads to Paradise; and obscene speech is part of harshness, and harshness leads to Hell."
"3200","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Modesty and faith are joined together; so when one of them is taken away, the other is taken away as well."
"3201","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Modesty and reticence in speech are two branches of faith, and obscene speech and boastful eloquence are two branches of hypocrisy."
"3202","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Modesty brings nothing but good."
"3203","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Snakes are the transformed form of the jinn, just as apes and swine were transformed from among the Children of Israel."
"3204","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""The snake is a harmful creature, the scorpion is a harmful creature, the mouse is a harmful creature, and the crow is a harmful creature."
